    "K_t": "Evidence:\n[1] Word board games are those games played on a board as players of the game attempt to construct words that use a scoring system.\n[2] Totopoly is a commercial board game, based on the events leading up to, and during, a horse race.\n[3] The objective of the game is to mount profitable expeditions to one or more of the five lost cities (the Himalayas, the Brazilian Rain Forest, the Desert Sands, the Ancient Volcanos and Neptune's Realm).\n[4] David Parlett (born 1939) is a games scholar, historian, and translator from South London, who has studied both card games and board games. His published works include many popular books on games and the more academic volumes \"The Oxford Guide to Card Games\" and \"The Oxford History of Board Games\", both now out of print."
